    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d66">

                <pb facs="0121" n="39" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg39"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President’s Special Assistant</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the President
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d66-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-24">January 24,
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Nr 2064 to Map Room White House from Harry Hopkins. Send following to
                    President.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“Have had very satisfactory visit London. Leaving for Paris tomorrow.
                        Churchill well. He says that if we had spent ten years on research, we could
                        not have found a worse place in the world than <pb facs="0122" n="40"
                            xml:id="pg40"/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Magneto</hi> but that he feels that he can
                        survive it by bringing an adequate supply of whisky. He claims it is good
                        for typhus and deadly on lice which thrive in those parts. Sorry to hear
                        that Watson seasick as usual. Regards to all. Signed Harry.”</p>
                </quote>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d66-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d66-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the United States Military Attaché, London, via Army channels.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
